{"author":"cursor[bot]","body":"### Pre-prompt state JSON tag rename lacks backward compatibility

**Low Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
The `PrePromptState` JSON tag changed from `"last_transcript_line_count"` to `"step_transcript_start"` without any backward-compatible migration or deprecated fallback field. If a pre-prompt state file was written by the old CLI (with `last_transcript_line_count`), and then read by the new CLI, `StepTranscriptStart` silently defaults to 0. This causes the stop handler to fall back to session state for `transcriptOffset` and pass 0 as `transcriptLinesAtStart` for token usage calculation, potentially overcounting tokens. Unlike `session.State` which has `NormalizeAfterLoad()` migration, `PrePromptState` has no equivalent.
<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->

